<title>MEXICO: Mexico needs to hike coffee output yields - Ag Min.</title>
<headline>Mexico needs to hike coffee output yields - Ag Min.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican Agriculture Minister Francisco Labastida Ochoa said the country needs to raise coffee productivity to boost foreign export incomes.</p>
<p>In a statement obtained Tuesday, the Agriculture Ministry said Lastida told a farmers' meeting that yields of 20 quintals (100-lb or 46 kg) bags per hectare should be reached instead of the 3-to-5-bag yields currently achieved.</p>
<p>Labastida said low yields were rife through Mexico's 12 coffee producing states across 250,000 hectares. He also said Mexico could use better systems of coffee trading.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530. E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com))</p>
</text>
